  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 351 AM EDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nIn the near term, a few showers were ongoing in SE parts of the\narea associated with a weak disturbance. Also monitoring\nfog/stratus development with vsbys near or below 1/2SM in NE\nareas and more hit and miss in others, focused on areas where\nrainfall occurred. Will be closely monitoring over the next\nseveral hours for possible dense fog headlines.\n\nOtherwise, Frontal boundary has become even more diffuse across\nthe region. Additional disturbances will continue to advect NE \ninto a moist, modestly unstable atmosphere during peak heating \nto bring widely scattered showers and storms to some areas. \nWhile widespread heavy rain is not expected, as was noted \nyesterday the slow movement and repeated training in a few areas\ncan quickly lead to local 2 to 4 inch rain totals. Will \nmaintain slgt chc to chc pops again into this evening to handle \nthe expected coverage. \n\nA somewhat stronger trough and cold front will move in Saturday\nwith another chance for some showers and storms. In the wake of\nthis trough a very brief lull in precip will occur Sat night\ninto at least the first parts of Sunday before the front returns\nback north across the area and then stall, potentially setting\nthe stage for multiple rounds of showers and thunderstorms late\nSunday into Tuesday. Plenty of moisture will remain in place to\nbring concerns for heavy rainfall, with models showing some\nincreased consistency in portions of IL/IN seeing a greater\nthreat for excessive rainfall. As a result, the forecast has\nbeen upgraded to a Slight risk for Sunday and Monday. Although\nthe signals have increased, not by any means a slam dunk as\nsimilar setups in past weeks have not fully transpired as timing\nof waves and location of the front are always tricky to pin down\nthis far out.",
